                <pb facs="0540" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1679: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-19T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                                1925—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>74. Embassy’s No. 118, November 12, 3 p.m. I should be glad to have you discuss
                    matter in friendly informal way with Chilean Minister for Foreign Affairs. This
                    will give him opportunity of his own volition to correct the existing abuses.
                    Continue to keep Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
